  "note": "Proves the one past rule on the non--ać verbs: robić, mówić, lubić, pić. mieć and chcieć are taught as WHOLE FORMS (miał-, chciał-) — no e→a rule slide, no contrast drill, no explanation of the shift (James 2026-08-04, deliberate load-split). SINGULAR ONLY — plural past is a2_past_plural. IMPERFECTIVE ONLY — no perfective twins, no aspect talk (that is a2_aspect). Full both-gender production; (m)/(f) cue convention as in a2_past_byc. Conservative choice: no forms borrowed from a2_past_ac, so this pack stands alone if the -ać unit is re-cut. ty-forms (mówiłeś/-aś, lubiłeś/-aś, piłeś/-aś) are shown in a table and tagged but not drilled here — they are drilled in a2_past_gym, which demands them.",
  "focus_structures": [
    "past_rest"
  ],
  "teaches_structures": [
    "past_rest"
  ],
  "uses_structures": [
    "past_rest",
    "past_byc",
    "miec_acc",
    "poss_nom",
    "question",
    "present_e_esz"
  ],
  "intro": [
    {
      "title": "One rule, every verb",
      "title_pl": "Jedna zasada",
      "body": "The past rule does not change from verb to verb. It is the same three steps every time:\n\n1. take the infinitive · 2. cut off -ć · 3. add -ł and the person ending.\n\nrobić → robi- → robi + ł → robiłem.\n\nThe endings are the ones you already have from był / byłem. Nothing new to learn there — only the stem in front of them changes.",
      "body_pl": "Bezokolicznik minus -ć, plus -ł, plus końcówka osoby. robić → robiłem.",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Form",
          "Meaning",
          "Used by / for"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "robiłem",
            "I was doing",
            "man speaking (m)"
          ],
          [
            "robiłam",
            "I was doing",
            "woman speaking (f)"
          ],
          [
            "robiłeś",
            "you were doing",
            "to a man (m)"
          ],
          [
            "robiłaś",
            "you were doing",
            "to a woman (f)"
          ],
          [
            "robił",
            "he was doing",
            "on · tata, brat"
          ],
          [
            "robiła",
            "she was doing",
            "ona · mama, siostra"
          ],
          [
            "robiło",
            "it was doing",
            "ono · dziecko"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Three more verbs, same cut",
      "title_pl": "Trzy kolejne czasowniki",
      "body": "Cut -ć off each infinitive and look at what is left: mówić → mówi-, lubić → lubi-, pić → pi-. Then -ł and the ending, exactly as before.\n\npić is the short one. Cut -ć and only pi- remains, so the past is piłem, piłam, pił, piła — short, but built by the same rule.",
      "body_pl": "mówi- / lubi- / pi- + ł + końcówka.",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Infinitive",
          "I … (m)",
          "I … (f)",
          "he …",
          "she …"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "mówić — to say, to speak",
            "mówiłem",
            "mówiłam",
            "mówił",
            "mówiła"
          ],
          [
            "lubić — to like",
            "lubiłem",
            "lubiłam",
            "lubił",
            "lubiła"
          ],
          [
            "pić — to drink",
            "piłem",
            "piłam",
            "pił",
            "piła"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Talking to someone",
      "title_pl": "Forma ty",
      "body": "The you endings are the pair you already type on robiłeś / robiłaś and byłeś / byłaś: -eś to a man, -aś to a woman. They sit on these stems unchanged.",
      "body_pl": "Końcówki -eś (do mężczyzny) i -aś (do kobiety).",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Infinitive",
          "you … (m)",
          "you … (f)"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "mówić — to say, to speak",
            "mówiłeś",
            "mówiłaś"
          ],
          [
            "lubić — to like",
            "lubiłeś",
            "lubiłaś"
          ],
          [
            "pić — to drink",
            "piłeś",
            "piłaś"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "Were you drinking coffee? (to a man)",
          "pl": "Piłeś kawę?"
        },
        {
          "en": "Did you like the music? (to a woman)",
          "pl": "Lubiłaś muzykę?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Two to learn whole",
      "title_pl": "Dwa czasowniki do zapamiętania",
      "body": "mieć (to have) and chcieć (to want) are the two you learn as whole words rather than build. Their past stems are miał- and chciał-. Learn those two stems and you are done — the endings on them are the ordinary ones.",
      "body_pl": "mieć → miał-, chcieć → chciał-. Uczymy się w całości.",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Infinitive",
          "I … (m)",
          "I … (f)",
          "he …",
          "she …"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "mieć — to have",
            "miałem",
            "miałam",
            "miał",
            "miała"
          ],
          [
            "chcieć — to want",
            "chciałem",
            "chciałam",
            "chciał",
            "chciała"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Children and things: -o",
      "title_pl": "Rodzaj nijaki: -o",
      "body": "Neuter nouns (dziecko, piwo, mleko) take -o on the past verb — the same -o you already use in było. No ending = he, -a = she, -o = it.",
      "body_pl": "Rodzaj nijaki: końcówka -o, tak jak w było.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "The child had milk.",
          "pl": "Dziecko miało mleko."
        },
        {
          "en": "The child was making breakfast.",
          "pl": "Dziecko robiło śniadanie."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
